WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.003
We start with three ideas: more free time, Japanese content, and fan behavior.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:10.461
These are business hypotheses, not proof of demand or future revenue.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:16.066
The seed round will test them through verified use, return behavior, and payments.

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:20.806
Automation may give some people more free time in some markets.

00:00:20.836 --> 00:00:26.276
Our hypothesis is that some of that time will move toward interactive entertainment.

00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:31.025
We must track the rate of change, audience size, and spending.

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:35.424
Japanese anime already has audiences and communities across many markets.

00:00:35.454 --> 00:00:39.738
People do more than watch. They remember, compare, and share.

00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:45.208
Interest differs by title, region, and generation, so we must measure each segment.

00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:50.892
A Japanese company may reduce language friction and business-practice friction in licensing talks.

00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:56.042
That is a working advantage, not evidence that a license will be granted.

00:00:56.072 --> 00:01:00.798
Trust must be earned through rights compliance, reporting, and operating results.

00:01:00.898 --> 00:01:06.048
Original animation cels are finite physical materials. They cannot simply be remade.

00:01:06.078 --> 00:01:10.370
Being rare does not determine authenticity, rights, liquidity, or price.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.000
We intend to preserve these materials. Business use starts only after rights approval.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.540
A quiz creates a score. That score sets the league ranking.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:26.511
Initial points are free. They cannot be transferred. Users earn them only from sponsor advertising quizzes.

00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:30.861
Players can compete on knowledge. They cannot buy or cash out points.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:35.242
We plan a future prediction feature using non-cash competition points.

00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:40.866
Each question would show its source and decision time, plus invalidation conditions, in advance.

00:01:40.896 --> 00:01:46.069
A version using money is not approved. Its release has not been decided.

00:01:46.169 --> 00:01:51.744
We should start now because content, behavior, and timing can be tested together.

00:01:51.774 --> 00:01:56.414
Judge the company by acquisition and retention, support, and sponsor evidence.

00:01:56.444 --> 00:01:59.887
If results miss the target, we postpone expansion.
